  "raw_text": "Step 1: Expand the product of the two polynomials $(3t^2 + 5t + a)(4t^2 + bt - 2)$.\n\nStep 2: Distribute each term in the first polynomial to each term in the second polynomial:\n\\[ = 3t^2(4t^2 + bt - 2) + 5t(4t^2 + bt - 2) + a(4t^2 + bt - 2) \\]\n\nStep 3: Perform the multiplication for each term:\n\\[ = 12t^4 + 3bt^3 - 6t^2 + 20t^3 + 5bt^2 - 10t + 4at^2 + abt - 2a \\]\n\nStep 4: Combine like terms:\n\\[ = 12t^4 + (3b + 20)t^3 + (-6 + 5b + 4a)t^2 + (-10 + ab)t - 2a \\]\n\nStep 5: Compare the coefficients of the expanded form with the given polynomial $12t^4 + 26t^3 - 8t^2 - 16t + 6$ to find the values of $a$ and $b$.\n\nStep 6: From the coefficient of $t^3$, we have:\n\\[ 3b + 20 = 26 \\]\n\\[ 3b = 6 \\]\n\\[ b = 2 \\]\n\nStep 7: From the coefficient of $t^2$, we have:\n\\[ -6 + 5b + 4a = -8 \\]\nSubstitute $b = 2$:\n\\[ -6 + 5(2) + 4a = -8 \\]\n\\[ -6 + 10 + 4a = -8 \\]\n\\[ 4 + 4a = -8 \\]\n\\[ 4a = -12 \\]\n\\[ a = -3 \\]\n\nStep 8: Calculate $a + b$:\n\\[ a + b = -3 + 2 = -1 \\]\n\nFinal answer: \\boxed{-1}<|im_end|>",
